ntervention. RESULTS A tendency was seen toward a lower 24-h EE with the MUFA than with the LF diet (P = 0.0675), but 
this trend did not remain after adjustment for the initial loses of fat mass and fat-free mass (P = 0.2963). 
Meal-induced thermogenesis was significantly (P < 0.05) lower with the MUFA than with the LF diet, but no time x 
