plasma triglyceride concentrations (by 0.21 (0.09) mmol/l, P < 0.05, for low total fat diet; by 0.39 (0.15) mmol/l, P < 
0.05, for high unsaturated fat diet), while high density lipoprotein cholesterol concentrations after fasting and plasma
glucose and insulin concentrations during test meals were not modified by either diet. CONCLUSIONS Both test diets are  
suitable (alone or in combination) for treatment of hypercholesterolaemia."}, {"study_index": 304, "title": "Effects of 
