tailored nutrition counseling intervention study for lowering cardiovascular risk. Fat intake 15 mo before the          
assessment of psychosocial determinants was used as a measure of habit. We used logistic regression analyses to develop 
a model predicting intention to change fat consumption. RESULTS Our regression model explained 43% of the variance in   
intention. Patients who perceived higher subjective norm or more social support had a higher intention. Habit was a     
significant predictor of intention in interaction with self-efficacy and health threat. Attitude, health threat, age,   
and group membership (ie, whether patients had been in the intervention group or the control group of the intervention  
study) were also included in the regression model. CONCLUSIONS The results suggest that habit in addition to subjective 
