decreased, compared with baseline, by 9%, 19%, 17%, and 25%, respectively. At week 210, serum total cholesterol/HDL-C 
ratio was 8% less than week 0. Compared with baseline, triglyceride levels decreased significantly by 21%, 31%, 29%, and
29% at weeks 34, 54, 104, and 139, respectively. At week 210, triglyceride levels were 16% below baseline. Total 
