lipoprotein changes were qualitatively similar between men and women. However, greater decreases in serum total 
cholesterol, LDL-C, and triglyceride levels were observed in participants with high (n = 10) compared with low (n = 10) 
baseline lipid levels. Cholesterol changes were not affected by anorexiant medications. However, triglyceride levels at 
week 34 were significantly (p less than 0.025) less in the participants treated with anorexiants.(ABSTRACT TRUNCATED AT 
